</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="S4.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">This diagram illustrates the impact of varying latent dimensions on the posterior samples. The circular dots represent the variational formulation of the forward KL divergence and the hollow squares correspond to the Sinkhorn divergence. The x-axis shows latent dimension and the y-axis shows <math id="S4.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-distance between true and generated end-effector positions.
</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
