<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Background</h2>

<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rademacher Complexity)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a class of real-valued functions over the domain <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{n}\overset{i.i.d.}{\sim}P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{n}\overset{i.i.d.}{\sim}P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> denote an i.i.d. dataset. With <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. Rademacher random variables (i.e., <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> w.p. <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> each), we define the Rademacher complexity of the function class <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
</div>
</div>
